        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Decision Rule"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stream a transformation: plain pipe",
            "Capture a small scalar: `$()`",
            "Fan out one stream: `tee` + `>()`",
            "Coordinate processes: `mkfifo`",
            "Need re-read or seek: `mktemp` file"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Buffering Ladder",
          "text": "Pipe 64 KB, `$()` unbounded RAM, FIFO 64 KB, file disk-backed. Match the plumbing to the data volume."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Failure Visibility"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$()` hides child status entirely",
            "Pipes report last stage unless `pipefail`",
            "FIFO ends fail independently — check each hop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "set -o pipefail",
            "cmd | tee log | grep -i err",
            "rc=$?    # first failure wins"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cost and Portability"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "All of it is copies through kernel buffers",
            "Fewer hops, fewer forks win hot loops",
            "`|`, `$()`, `mkfifo`: POSIX. `<()`: bash/ksh/zsh",
            "FIFO blocking details vary by system",
            "`$()` as args caps near 2 MB; piping doesn't"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Choosing the Right Plumbing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "`cmd <(other)` vs `cmd < <(other)`?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "First passes a path argument",
            "Second feeds stdin from the stream",
            "One character, different plumbing"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "wc -l <(ls)    # path argument",
            "wc -l < <(ls)  # stdin fed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Core Job",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`tee` reads stdin and writes every byte to stdout plus each file. `cmd | tee run.log` keeps the pipeline visible."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "cmd",
              "tee",
              "run.log",
              "stdout"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sinks and Modes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`tee -a` appends; bare `tee` truncates at open",
            "`tee f1 f2 f3`: identical bytes everywhere",
            "`tee file > /dev/null`: capture silently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "cmd | tee >(gzip > c.gz) \\",
            "          >(sha256sum > c.sha)",
            "# live compress + hash branches"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Status and Signals"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`set -o pipefail` or failing targets hide",
            "`head` exits early → `tee` takes SIGPIPE 13",
            "Tail of the data silently lost",
            "GNU `tee -p` keeps writing, reports errors"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The sudo Redirect Bug",
          "items": [
            "`sudo cmd > /root/f`: your shell redirects",
            "File opened unprivileged — denied",
            "`sudo cmd | sudo tee /root/f` writes correctly"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "sudo cmd > /root/f    # shell redirects",
            "sudo cmd | sudo tee /root/f"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Probe and Price"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`cmd1 | tee /dev/stderr | cmd2`: mid-pipe probe",
            "Every sink is a full duplicate write",
            "Three sinks triple the write syscalls",
            "Don't fan out casually on hot paths"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "make 2>&1 | tee build.log | grep -i error",
            "# failures live, full log kept"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Copying Tap",
          "text": "`tee` duplicates bytes, not references. Each destination pays full writes — spend visibility where it matters."
        },
