    {
      "page_title": "xargs: Input Stream to Command Lines",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Golden Pair"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "find . -name cache -print0 |",
            "  xargs -0 rm",
            "# NUL: spaces/quotes harmless"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Quotes, spaces, newline bytes wreck bare parsing",
            "Only `-0` or an explicit `-d` is safe"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Batching and Parallelism"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Default: pack items per invocation to `ARG_MAX`",
            "`-P 8`: up to 8 concurrent invocations",
            "Split input with `-n` or `-L` chunks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "find queue -type f -print0 |",
            "  xargs -0 -n 20 -P 8 process_job"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Templates and Shells"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`-I {}`: fixed position, one run each — slow",
            "Multi-command: `xargs -I{} sh -c 'a {}; b {}'`",
            "Children get no stdin — xargs consumed it",
            "Pipe data through `xargs cat` instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Surprise Drawer",
          "items": [
            "GNU runs once on empty input — pass `-r`",
            "BSD/macOS skips empty, lacks `-r`",
            "Exit 123: at least one child failed",
            "`-t` prints lines, `-p` asks first"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Argument Pump",
          "text": "`xargs` turns a byte stream into command lines. Without NUL delimiters it guesses — and filenames lose."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why did `find | xargs rm` delete the wrong thing?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`my file` split into two names",
            "Quote chars parsed as syntax",
            "Always pair `-print0` with `-0`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Counter Bug",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "n=0",
            "cat f | while read l; do",
            "  n=$((n+1))",
            "done",
            "echo \"$n\"   # 0 — subshell"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every pipe element — the loop included — runs in a subshell. Its variables die at `done`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Fixes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# fix 1: redirect input",
            "while read l; do n=$((n+1)); done < f",
            "# fix 2: process substitution",
            "while read l; do :; done < <(cmd)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "cat f | while",
                "lines": [
                  "subshell",
                  "counters lost",
                  "status lost"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "while < f",
                "lines": [
                  "current shell",
                  "vars persist",
                  "status visible"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Robust read"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`IFS= read -r l`: keeps whitespace, no escapes",
            "No trailing newline? Guard: `|| [[ -n $l ]]`",
            "Variable lines: `done <<< $var` here-string"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "find . -print0 |",
