          "type": "heading",
          "text": "stdio Buffering"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "To pipe or file: fully buffered, 4–8 KB flushes",
            "To a terminal: line buffered",
            "Pipeline logs lag for exactly this reason"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "stdbuf -oL cmd | tail -f log",
            "grep --line-buffered err | sink",
            "# or flush inside the program"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "SIGPIPE"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Writing with no readers raises signal 13",
            "Default: the writer dies silently",
            "`yes | head`: head quits, yes dies — self-clean"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "yes | head -n 10   # yes killed: 13",
            "set -o pipefail    # rightmost nonzero rc"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "EOF Discipline",
          "items": [
            "EOF arrives when every write end closes",
            "A stray inherited fd hides EOF, hangs `wc`",
            "Close what you open: `exec 3>&-`",
            "Inspect: `lsof`, `fuser`, `strace`"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Backpressure",
          "text": "A full pipe blocks the writer — nothing buffers without bound except `$()` and files. Backpressure is built-in flow control."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fork Economics"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every stage and every `<()` is one process",
            "Hundreds in a loop dwarf the real work",
            "Batch instead of forking per line"
          ]
        }
      ]
